**What changed**

- [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:938): new `dsg__visible_of` helper (with a `data/map?` fast path so non-map values skip the decode entirely). Bound in the prelude at [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2825).
- [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:948): `dsg__condition_wrapper` normalizes its visible slot through `dsg__visible_of`, so a wrapper never nests another wrapper as its visible value. The wrapper-as-cell design, witness, and `dsg__condition_retained` are untouched in structure.
- [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:956): P3 shape-guard in `condition-retained-form` — the candidate must be cell-ref shaped (`:type :cell-ref`, `:id`, `:seal`, 64-char string seal) before `cell/authentic?` is asked, mirroring `dsg__admitted?`; the contents 3-vector check remains before the witness comparison. One deviation from the brief's literal ordering: I did **not** move the `cell/get` contents read before `cell/authentic?`, because that aborts forged cell-shaped payloads with a dead-or-forged abort instead of returning nil (proven by the existing collision-literal test failing under that ordering). The shape guard gives the same fail-closed discipline without the abort.
- [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1815): guest `=`/`==` unwrap every operand, guest `get` and native predicates (`nil?`, `empty?`, `data/map?`, `data/vector?`, `data/string?`, `data/number?`, `data/callable?`, `data/contains?`) unwrap the collection operand, and keyword lookups `(:k e)` unwrap the map operand — all at `compile-av-application`, so every position (tail or operand) is covered.
- [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1274): library predicates (`map?`, `vector?`, `set?`, `seq?`, `coll?`, `sequential?`, `list?`, `string?`, `boolean?`, `int?`, `keyword?`, `symbol?`, `var?`, `fn?`, `reduced?`, plus `contains?`) unwrap their argument in `lower-tail`'s guest branch. `throw`, `assoc`, and `cell/set!` are deliberately **not** routed, so rethrow and saved-rethrow still forward the retained condition.

**Identity semantics now guaranteed**

A caught value `e` remains the authenticated wrapper cell, so `(throw e)` and `(cell/set! saved e)` + `(throw (cell/get saved))` forward the original condition byte-identical. But every guest observation of `e` — `=`, `get`, keyword lookup, the predicates above, `ex-message`, `.getMessage`, `ex-data` — answers as if `e` were the original payload `dsg__visible`: `(= e original)` is true even when `original` is a `cell/new` value, `(:yin.k/cause e)`/`(:yin.k/message e)`/`(:code (ex-data e))` read the payload, and `(:yang.call/reason e)` reads a caught protocol condition. `dsg__visible_of` is the identity on any non-wrapper value.

**Tests**

New [test-exception-r3-caught-payload-identity](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1595) (20 assertions, both lanes): `(= e orig)` across a dynamic call for a location-independent map and an ex-info payload; `(= e original)` with a `cell/new` payload; `(:yin.k/cause e)`, `(:yin.k/message e)`, `(get e :yin.k/data)`, custom key `(:code (ex-data e))`, `map?`/`vector?`/`string?` predicates; `(:yang.call/reason e)` on a protocol condition; nested capture → rethrow across a dynamic call → `(ex-message e2)` plus payload equality; and a cross-language guard where a catch receives a `:yang.call/thrown` condition whose value is location-independent. It failed 17/20 assertions pre-fix and passes post-fix. `yang.call.exception-contract-test` was not run, per the brief (shiva-only).

